            <ArticleTitle>Neuroleptic malignant syndrome: case report and review.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>355-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neuroleptic malignant syndrome is a rare but potentially fatal disorder that has been associated with the use of antipsychotic medications. Because neuroleptic malignant syndrome is rare, clinicians often have a low index of suspicion for the disorder which may lead to delayed treatment and increased mortality. This article describes a case of neuroleptic malignant syndrome and briefly reviews current diagnostic criteria and treatment options.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
